course: dictionary
lesson: 2032
title: Conflict: a clash, a problem or a war
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A conflict is a serious disagreement or argument between people. It can also be a war or fight between countries or groups. In a story, the conflict is the main problem the characters must face, and the resolution is how that problem gets solved.
explain: Look at the words around it. «After years of conflict, the Good Friday Agreement of 1998 brought peace.» Peace came after the conflict, so conflict here means fighting and trouble between groups, not a small squabble. Peace is the opposite of conflict, which is another clue.
explain: Conflict can also be a verb. When two things conflict, they cannot both be true or happen at the same time. Test it: swap in "clash" and see if the sentence still makes sense. Phrases to know: in conflict with, conflict resolution (solving arguments calmly), and conflicting advice (advice that points in different directions).
fact: A conflict is a serious disagreement or argument.
fact: A conflict can also be a war or fight between countries or groups.
fact: «Conflict» is the official, softer word for a war.
fact: If two things conflict, they cannot both be true or happen at the same time.
fact: A conflict of interest happens when someone's own reasons could stop them being fair or honest.
exercise: «After years of conflict, the Good Friday Agreement of 1998 brought peace.» What does conflict mean here? | A small game of cards | A long holiday by the sea | *A serious disagreement or fighting between groups | Happy celebrations for the whole town
exercise: Ellie has two clubs on Tuesday at the same time. What does it mean that the clubs conflict? | They are both in the same park | They have the same name | *They cannot both happen at the same time
exercise: In a story, what is the conflict? | The name of the author | *The main problem the characters must face | The picture on the cover | The last page of the book
test: Which word is the official, softer word for a war? | Feast | *Conflict | Festival | Holiday
test: A judge's friend is taking part in the case. What is this called? | A tie-break game | A birthday party | *A conflict of interest
exam: Ravi's grandad gives him conflicting advice: one says stay in, one says go out. What does conflicting advice mean? | Advice written in a book | Advice given by a friend only | *Advice that points in two different directions | The same advice said twice
